"""
Document Ingestion & Search Engine
==================================
Ingests PDF, CSV and XLSX files, splits them into chunks, embeds each chunk with a sentence-embedding
model, and stores the vectors in Qdrant. Search embeds the query and returns the closest chunks, with
optional metadata filters (file type, source file, category).

Stack: FastAPI, sentence-transformers, Qdrant, PyMuPDF, pandas (XLSX), openpyxl.

Install:   pip install fastapi "uvicorn[standard]" python-multipart sentence-transformers \\
                       "qdrant-client>=1.10" pymupdf pandas openpyxl
Run:       uvicorn main:app            (or: python main.py)
Test:      pip install httpx && python -m unittest test_main -v

Configuration (environment variables)
  QDRANT_URL                    Qdrant server URL. Unset: an in-memory store (data is lost on restart).
  QDRANT_API_KEY                Qdrant API key, if the server requires one.
  COLLECTION_NAME               default "enterprise_documents"
  EMBEDDING_MODEL               default "all-MiniLM-L6-v2"
  API_KEY                       If set, /ingest, /search and /documents require the X-API-Key header.
  MAX_UPLOAD_MB                 default 50
  MAX_CHUNKS_PER_DOCUMENT       default 50000
  CHUNK_WORDS / CHUNK_OVERLAP   default 160 / 30 (see the note on model input length below)
  EMBED_BATCH_SIZE              default 64
  LOG_LEVEL                     default INFO

Endpoints
  POST   /ingest      multipart: file (pdf, csv, xlsx), optional custom_category
  POST   /search      JSON: query, limit, doc_type, source, category, score_threshold
  DELETE /documents   query: source=<filename>
  GET    /health

Notes
  * all-MiniLM-L6-v2 reads at most 256 word pieces per input and silently ignores the rest, so chunks
    must be short. The 160-word default fits; the engine warns at startup if the setting is too large.
  * Re-uploading a file with the same name replaces its earlier version; re-uploading identical content
    is a no-op. Point ids are deterministic, so retries cannot create duplicates.
  * Legacy .xls files are not supported (convert to .xlsx).
"""
